{title: 554 - O Let Me Walk With Thee}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[D7]O[G]let me walk with [Am]Thee, [D7]my [G]God,
As [Em]Enoch [C]walked in days of [G]old;
[G]Place Thou [G7]my [C]trembling [Cm]hand in [G]Thine,
And [C]sweet com[G]munion [D]with me [G]hold;
E’en [G7]though the [C]path I [Cm]may not [G]see,
[C]Yet, [G]Jesus, [D]let [D7]me [G]walk [D]with [G]Thee.

Verse 2:
[D7]I [G]cannot, [Am]dare [D7]not, [G]walk alone;
[Em]The tempest [C]rages in [G]the sky,
[G]A [G7]thousand [C]snares [Cm]beset [G]my feet,
[C]A [G]thousand foes [D]are [G]lurking nigh.
[G7]Still [C]Thou the [Cm]raging of [G]the sea,
[C]O [G]Master! [D]let [D7]me [G]walk [D]with [G]Thee.

Verse 3:
[D7]If [G]I may [Am]rest [D7]my hand [G]in Thine,
[Em]I'll count [C]the joys of [G]earth but loss,
[G]And [G7]firmly, [C]bravely [Cm]journey [G]on;
[C]I'll [G]bear the [D]banner of [G]the cross
[G7]Till [C]Zion's glorious [Cm]gates [G]I see;
[C]Yet, [G]Savior, [D]let [D7]me [G]walk [D]with [G]Thee.
